---
layout: layouts/base.njk
pagination:
  data: docs.families
  size: 1
  alias: family
  addAllPagesToCollections: true
permalink: "{{ family.tokensUrl }}"
eleventyComputed:
  title: "{{ family.name }} tokens"
  description: "{% if family.tokenSets | length %}The component tokens {{ family.name | lower }} reads, with their values in each mode. Override one to restyle it.{% else %}{{ family.name }} has no component tokens of its own: it is laid out with the spacing scale.{% endif %}"
---

{#
  A component's own tokens: the component tier of the token reference, shown
  with the component it belongs to rather than in one long list. The family's
  token sets come from _data/docs.js; the rows from _data/tokens.js, through the
  same table as the Tokens page.
#}

{% include "partials/component-header.njk" %}

{% set componentTier = tokens.tiers | findBy('tier', 'component') %}

{% if family.tokenSets | length %}
  <p>
    These are {{ family.name | lower }}'s public styling API. Each is a CSS
    variable the component reads, defined by
    <code>@quieto/design-tokens</code> and aliasing a semantic token, so it
    follows the theme. Overriding one is the supported way to restyle the
    component, on one instance or on a whole page:
  </p>

  <pre><code>.brand {{ family.primary.tagName }} {
  --{{ family.sampleToken }}: {{ family.sampleValue }};
}</code></pre>

  {% for set in family.tokenSets %}
    {% set group = componentTier.categories | findBy('category', set) %}
    <h2 id="tokens-{{ set }}"><code>{{ set }}</code> tokens <span class="tab-count">{{ group.tokens | length }}</span></h2>
    {% set rows = group.tokens %}
    {% include "partials/token-table.njk" %}
  {% endfor %}
{% else %}
  <p>
    {{ family.name }} has no component tokens of its own. It is laid out entirely
    with the <a href="/foundations/tokens/#token-reference">spacing scale</a>
    (<code>--qds-spacing-*</code>), which it reads directly.
  </p>
{% endif %}

<p>
  <a href="/foundations/tokens/">All primitive and semantic tokens</a> are on the
  Tokens page.
</p>

<script type="module" src="/assets/token-target.js"></script>
